FlyWeb port (not yet merged to M156): from branch-heads/8154 afa45b8e16 (M159 merge of 34e522970b). Applied after siguiente/chromium/0009 (main 041491e936), which it needs: without 0009 the MenuRunner released in GetDropCallback/OnMenuClosed is deleted synchronously and both upstream tests fail. Same code change as upstream; both menu_controller.cc hunks re-anchored by hand because 156 has DCHECK(drop_target) where 159 has CHECK(drop_target, base::NotFatalUntil::M163). The two tests are upstream verbatim (the view_tracker.h include they need comes from 0009, as in upstream). Moved here from portes-159/chromium/0001 on 21-11. No brave-core patches or chromium_src for these files.

Original change's description:
> views: Fix FOR_DROP menu drag and drop teardown UAF
>
> Add ScopedDeletionGuard to MenuController::GetDropCallback so
> MenuRunner and SubmenuView destruction is deferred until GetDropCallback
> unwinds, and return DRAG_NONE from MenuController::OnDragUpdated when
> destruction is pending.
